/-!
# The formal sections of `k[x,y][[s,t]]/(xs-yt)` away from the origin

Let `k` be a field, let `A = k[x,y][[s,t]]/(xs - yt)`, let `I = (s,t)` and let
`𝔞 = (x,y,s,t)`. On `X = Spec(A) ∖ V(𝔞)` put `ℱₙ = 𝒪_X/Iⁿ𝒪_X`. Stacks 0EH8 observes
that the rational function

`g = t/x = s/y`

is regular on an open neighbourhood `V ⊆ X` of `V(I𝒪_X)`, so each power `gᵉ` is a formal
section — an element of `M = lim H⁰(X, ℱₙ)` — that `gᵉ → 0` in the limit topology on `M`
because `gᵉ` dies in `ℱₑ`, that nevertheless `gᵉ ∉ IM` for every `e`, and that
`cd(A, I) = 2`. Since Stacks 0EH7 says the limit topology on `lim Hᵖ(X, ℱₙ)` is `I`-adic as
soon as `cd(A, I) = 1`, the example shows that hypothesis is sharp.

This file carries the ring, the ideals, the rational function and the cohomological
dimension.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Examples.NonAdicLimit.exampleRing` — the ring `A = k[x,y][[s,t]]/(xs - yt)`,
  with `coordX`, `coordY`, `coordS`, `coordT` its four coordinates.
* `Stacks.Examples.NonAdicLimit.adicIdeal`, `.puncturingIdeal` — the ideals `I = (s,t)` and
  `𝔞 = (x,y,s,t)`.
* `Stacks.Examples.NonAdicLimit.rationalFunctionAwayX`, `.rationalFunctionAwayY` — the two
  charts `t/x` and `s/y` of `g`, as explicit elements of `A[1/x]` and `A[1/y]`. They are
  honest terms, not choices extracted from an existence statement.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Examples.NonAdicLimit.notMem_or_notMem_of_adicIdeal_le` — every point of `X` at
  which `I` vanishes lies in `D(x) ∪ D(y)`; this is the neighbourhood `V` of `V(I𝒪_X)`
  on which `g` is regular.
* `Stacks.Examples.NonAdicLimit.coordX_mul_rationalFunctionAwayX`,
  `.coordY_mul_rationalFunctionAwayY`, `.rationalFunctionAway_eq_of_isUnit` — `g` is regular
  on each of the two charts, with `x·g = t` and `y·g = s`, and the two charts agree wherever
  both `x` and `y` are invertible. Together these are the assertion `g = t/x = s/y`.
* `Stacks.Examples.NonAdicLimit.pow_rationalFunctionAwayX_mem_map_pow`,
  `.pow_rationalFunctionAwayY_mem_map_pow` — on each chart `gᵉ` lies in `Iⁿ` for every
  `n ≤ e`. This is the computation behind `gᵉ → 0`.
* `Stacks.Examples.NonAdicLimit.cohomologicalDimension_adicIdeal_eq_two` — `cd(A, I) = 2`.
* `Stacks.Examples.NonAdicLimit.sectionG_pow_mem_idealPowerMultiple` — `gᵉ ∈ Iⁿ·M` near the
  formal locus, on all of `D(x) ∪ D(y)`, for `n ≤ e`.
* `Stacks.Examples.NonAdicLimit.formalSectionG` — `gᵉ` as an element of
  `M = lim H⁰(X, ℱₙ)` itself, via the comparison map of Stacks 0EG2.
* `Stacks.Examples.NonAdicLimit.tendsto_formalSectionG_atTop_nhds_zero` — `gᵉ → 0` in the
  limit topology on `M`.
* `Stacks.Examples.NonAdicLimit.formalLimitModuleCat`,
  `.formalSectionGModule`, `.adicIdealSmulFormalLimit` — `M` with its `Γ(X, 𝒪_X)`-module
  structure, `gᵉ` as an element of it, and `I·M` as a genuine `Submodule`;
  `.NotMemAdicIdealSmulFormalLimit` is the clause `gᵉ ∉ I·M`, which these make statable, and it
  is proved as `Stacks.Examples.NonAdicLimit.notMemAdicIdealSmulFormalLimit` in
  `StacksFrontier/Examples/Completion/NonAdicLimitNotAdic.lean`.
* `Stacks.Examples.NonAdicLimit.tendsto_formalSectionGModule_atTop_nhds_zero` — `gᵉ → 0` read
  on that module-valued limit, so that both halves of 0EH8's conclusion speak of one `M`.

## Implementation notes

The ring is built as `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k)` modulo the principal
ideal generated by `xs - yt`, so that `x = X 0` and `y = X 1` are the polynomial coordinates
and `s = X 0`, `t = X 1` the power-series ones.

`cd(A, I) ≤ 2` is Stacks 0DX9: `I` has two generators. For `cd(A, I) ≥ 2` the ring is
specialized along `x, y ↦ 0`, which kills the relation and presents `A/(x,y)` as
`k[[s]][[t]]`; there `I` becomes the maximal ideal, whose cohomological dimension is the
Krull dimension by Stacks 0DXE, and that dimension is at least two. Extending an ideal along
a ring map cannot raise the cohomological dimension (Stacks 0DXA), which gives the bound back
on `A`.

**What is here, of the module-level assertions.** `g` is glued from the two charts above into
a section of `𝒪_X` on `D(x) ∪ D(y)` (`sectionG`), each power `gᵉ` is shown to lie in `Iⁿ·M`
near the formal locus for `n ≤ e` (`sectionG_pow_mem_idealPowerMultiple`, glued from the two
charts via `AlgebraicGeometry.mem_submodule_of_locally_mem`), `gᵉ` is read off as an element of
`M = lim H⁰(X, ℱₙ)` itself through the comparison map of Stacks 0EG2 (`formalSectionG`), and
`gᵉ → 0` in the limit topology on `M` is proved
(`tendsto_formalSectionG_atTop_nhds_zero`), the limit topology written out as
`⨅ n, TopologicalSpace.induced (limit.π …) ⊥` since it has no name of its own in this library
(compare `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/FormalGeometry/AlgebraizationCoherentFormal/`).

`M` also carries its `Γ(X, 𝒪_X)`-module structure (`formalLimitModuleCat`), so that `I·M` is a
genuine `Submodule` (`adicIdealSmulFormalLimit`) and `gᵉ ∉ I·M` is a proposition that can be
written down (`NotMemAdicIdealSmulFormalLimit`). This is the same limit read in
`ModuleCat Γ(X, 𝒪_X)` instead of in `Ab`: the quotient tower is evaluated through
`SheafOfModules.evaluation` rather than through `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.toPresheaf`,
which changes the diagram not at all
(`Stacks.Algebraization.formalSectionsModule_comp_forget₂`), and `formalSectionG` is carried
across the resulting comparison of the two limits by
`Stacks.Algebraization.ofFormalSections`, which changes none of its components
(`Stacks.Algebraization.π_ofFormalSections`). Both halves of 0EH8's conclusion are therefore
available against one `M`: `gᵉ → 0` is `tendsto_formalSectionGModule_atTop_nhds_zero` there.

**The clause `gᵉ ∉ IM`.** This is proved, in
`StacksFrontier/Examples/Completion/NonAdicLimitNotAdic.lean`
(`Stacks.Examples.NonAdicLimit.notMemAdicIdealSmulFormalLimit`), and it completes the example:
with it, both of 0EH8's topological assertions hold of one and the same `M`, so the limit
topology on `M` differs from the `I`-adic one.

The source's own argument rests on a computation of `H⁰(U, ℱₙ)` that it marks "computation
omitted". The proof given does not compute those sections. It specializes the whole situation
along `ρ : A ⟶ R[x,y]`, `x ↦ x`, `y ↦ y`, `s ↦ y·z`, `t ↦ x·z` with `R = k[T]/(Tᵉ⁺¹)`, under
which `𝔞` lands in `(x,y)`, so the punctured plane `D(x) ∪ D(y) ⊆ Spec R[x,y]` maps to `X`, and
`I^(e+1)` lands in `0`, so that map factors through `ℱₑ₊₁`. Since the punctured plane carries no
function beyond the polynomials — this is where the codimension two of the removed locus, the
same fact as `cd(A, I) = 2`, enters — every formal section acquires a value in `R[x,y]`,
`A`-semilinearly over `ρ`. On `gᵉ` the value is `zᵉ`, forced by `xᵉ·gᵉ = tᵉ`; a decomposition
`gᵉ = s·m₁ + t·m₂` would instead make it `y z·(…) + x z·(…)`, which vanishes at `x = y = 0`
while `zᵉ ≠ 0`.

The truncated charts of `StacksFrontier/Examples/Completion/NonAdicLimitChart.lean`
(`Stacks.Examples.NonAdicLimit.chartTruncationEquivX` and `.chartTruncationEquivY`) are the
shape of the source's omitted computation itself: `A[1/x]/Iⁿ ≅ k[x^{±1}, y][t]/(tⁿ)` sending
`s ↦ (y/x)t`, hence `I ↦ (t)` and `g ↦ x⁻¹t`, and its `D(y)` twin. They rest on a power series
ring modulo a power of its ideal of variables being the polynomial ring modulo the same
(`Stacks.MvPowerSeries.RegularParameters.polynomialTruncationEquiv`) and on the change of
variables `s ↦ (y/x)t` eliminating `s` over a ring in which `x` is a unit
(`Stacks.TruncatedChart.chartEquiv`, with `Stacks.TruncatedChart.chartEquivSwap` for the twin).

The *untruncated* form `A[1/x] ≅ k[x^{±1}, y][[t]]`, which is the shape one first writes down,
is false — see the docstring of `not_isUnit_mul_add_mul` for why, and for why the truncation is
the true statement. Stacks 0EH7 itself is a separate tag.

Against `formalLimitModule` the clause `gᵉ ∉ I·M` cannot even be *written*, because
`formalSections` is `Ab`-valued, so its limit is a bare abelian group carrying no
`Module Γ(X, ⊤)` instance — which is what `I·M` needs in order to be a `Submodule`.
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/FormalGeometry/FormalSectionsModule.lean` supplies that module
structure, and `NotMemAdicIdealSmulFormalLimit` is the clause written against it.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EH8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EH8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EH7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EH7)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

universe u

namespace Stacks.Examples.NonAdicLimit

open Stacks.LocalCohomology

variable (k : Type u) [Field k]

/-! ### The ring -/

/-- `k[x,y][[s,t]]`, before the relation is imposed. -/
abbrev ambient : Type u := MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k)

/-- The polynomial coordinate `x` of `k[x,y][[s,t]]`. -/
def ambientX : ambient k := MvPowerSeries.C (MvPolynomial.X 0)

/-- The polynomial coordinate `y` of `k[x,y][[s,t]]`. -/
def ambientY : ambient k := MvPowerSeries.C (MvPolynomial.X 1)

/-- The power-series coordinate `s` of `k[x,y][[s,t]]`. -/
def ambientS : ambient k := MvPowerSeries.X 0

/-- The power-series coordinate `t` of `k[x,y][[s,t]]`. -/
def ambientT : ambient k := MvPowerSeries.X 1

/-- The element `xs - yt` of `k[x,y][[s,t]]`. -/
def relation : ambient k := ambientX k * ambientS k - ambientY k * ambientT k

/-- The ring `A = k[x,y][[s,t]]/(xs - yt)` of the example. -/
abbrev exampleRing : Type u := ambient k ⧸ Ideal.span {relation k}

/-- The image of the polynomial coordinate `x` in `A`. -/
def coordX : exampleRing k := Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (ambientX k)

/-- The image of the polynomial coordinate `y` in `A`. -/
def coordY : exampleRing k := Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (ambientY k)

/-- The image of the power-series coordinate `s` in `A`. -/
def coordS : exampleRing k := Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (ambientS k)

/-- The image of the power-series coordinate `t` in `A`. -/
def coordT : exampleRing k := Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (ambientT k)

/-- The defining relation of `A`: `xs = yt`. -/
theorem coordX_mul_coordS : coordX k * coordS k = coordY k * coordT k := by
  refine Ideal.Quotient.eq.mpr ?_
  exact Ideal.subset_span (by simp [relation])

/-- The ideal `I = (s,t)` of `A`. -/
def adicIdeal : Ideal (exampleRing k) := Ideal.span {coordS k, coordT k}

/-- The ideal `𝔞 = (x,y,s,t)` of `A`, whose zero locus is removed from `Spec(A)`. -/
def puncturingIdeal : Ideal (exampleRing k) :=
  Ideal.span {coordX k, coordY k, coordS k, coordT k}

/-- The coordinate `s` lies in `I = (s,t)`. -/
theorem coordS_mem_adicIdeal : coordS k ∈ adicIdeal k :=
  Ideal.subset_span (by simp)

/-- The coordinate `t` lies in `I = (s,t)`. -/
theorem coordT_mem_adicIdeal : coordT k ∈ adicIdeal k :=
  Ideal.subset_span (by simp)

/-- `I = (s,t)` is contained in `𝔞 = (x,y,s,t)`. -/
theorem adicIdeal_le_puncturingIdeal : adicIdeal k ≤ puncturingIdeal k := by
  rw [adicIdeal, Ideal.span_le]
  intro z hz
  simp only [Set.mem_insert_iff, Set.mem_singleton_iff] at hz
  rcases hz with rfl | rfl <;> exact Ideal.subset_span (by simp)

/-- The ideal `I = (s,t)` is finitely generated, by its two displayed generators. -/
theorem adicIdeal_fg : (adicIdeal k).FG := by
  classical
  exact ⟨{coordS k, coordT k}, by simp [adicIdeal]⟩

/-! ### The neighbourhood of `V(I𝒪_X)` -/

/-- **The neighbourhood `V` of Stacks 0EH8.** At every point of `X = Spec(A) ∖ V(𝔞)` at which
`I` vanishes, one of `x`, `y` is invertible: `V(I𝒪_X) ⊆ D(x) ∪ D(y)`. So `D(x) ∪ D(y)` is the
open neighbourhood of `V(I𝒪_X)` inside `X` on which the rational function `g = t/x = s/y`
below is regular. -/
@[stacks 0EH8 "the open neighbourhood V of V(I·O_X) in X on which t/x = s/y is regular is \
D(x) ∪ D(y)"]
theorem notMem_or_notMem_of_adicIdeal_le (p : PrimeSpectrum (exampleRing k))
    (hp : ¬ puncturingIdeal k ≤ p.asIdeal) (hI : adicIdeal k ≤ p.asIdeal) :
    coordX k ∉ p.asIdeal ∨ coordY k ∉ p.asIdeal := by
  by_contra hcon
  obtain ⟨hx, hy⟩ := not_or.mp hcon
  refine hp ?_
  rw [puncturingIdeal, Ideal.span_le]
  intro z hz
  simp only [Set.mem_insert_iff, Set.mem_singleton_iff] at hz
  rcases hz with rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl
  · exact not_not.mp hx
  · exact not_not.mp hy
  · exact hI (coordS_mem_adicIdeal k)
  · exact hI (coordT_mem_adicIdeal k)

/-! ### The rational function `g = t/x = s/y` -/

/-- The chart `t/x` of the rational function `g`, as an element of `A[1/x]`. -/
def rationalFunctionAwayX : Localization.Away (coordX k) :=
  IsLocalization.Away.invSelf (coordX k) *
    algebraMap (exampleRing k) (Localization.Away (coordX k)) (coordT k)

/-- The chart `s/y` of the rational function `g`, as an element of `A[1/y]`. -/
def rationalFunctionAwayY : Localization.Away (coordY k) :=
  IsLocalization.Away.invSelf (coordY k) *
    algebraMap (exampleRing k) (Localization.Away (coordY k)) (coordS k)

/-- **`g = t/x` on `D(x)`.** -/
@[stacks 0EH8 "the chart t/x of the rational function g, regular on D(x)"]
theorem coordX_mul_rationalFunctionAwayX :
    algebraMap (exampleRing k) (Localization.Away (coordX k)) (coordX k) *
        rationalFunctionAwayX k =
      algebraMap (exampleRing k) (Localization.Away (coordX k)) (coordT k) := by
  rw [rationalFunctionAwayX, ← mul_assoc, IsLocalization.Away.mul_invSelf, one_mul]

/-- **`g = s/y` on `D(y)`.** -/
@[stacks 0EH8 "the chart s/y of the rational function g, regular on D(y)"]
theorem coordY_mul_rationalFunctionAwayY :
    algebraMap (exampleRing k) (Localization.Away (coordY k)) (coordY k) *
        rationalFunctionAwayY k =
      algebraMap (exampleRing k) (Localization.Away (coordY k)) (coordS k) := by
  rw [rationalFunctionAwayY, ← mul_assoc, IsLocalization.Away.mul_invSelf, one_mul]

/-- **The two charts are the same rational function.** In any `A`-algebra in which `x` and `y`
are both invertible, an element solving `x·gx = t` and an element solving `y·gy = s` are
equal: `t/x = s/y`. -/
@[stacks 0EH8 "t/x = s/y: the two charts agree wherever x and y are both invertible"]
theorem rationalFunctionAway_eq_of_isUnit {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [Algebra (exampleRing k) R]
    (hx : IsUnit (algebraMap (exampleRing k) R (coordX k)))
    (hy : IsUnit (algebraMap (exampleRing k) R (coordY k)))
    (gx gy : R)
    (hgx : algebraMap (exampleRing k) R (coordX k) * gx =
      algebraMap (exampleRing k) R (coordT k))
    (hgy : algebraMap (exampleRing k) R (coordY k) * gy =
      algebraMap (exampleRing k) R (coordS k)) :
    gx = gy := by
  refine (hx.mul hy).mul_left_cancel ?_
  have hrel := congrArg (algebraMap (exampleRing k) R) (coordX_mul_coordS k)
  rw [map_mul, map_mul] at hrel
  linear_combination algebraMap (exampleRing k) R (coordY k) * hgx -
    algebraMap (exampleRing k) R (coordX k) * hgy - hrel

/-! ### `gᵉ` dies modulo `Iⁿ` for `n ≤ e` -/

/-- A multiple `c · zᵉ` of the `e`-th power of an element `z` of `I` lies in `Iⁿ·S` for
every `n ≤ e`. -/
private theorem mul_algebraMap_pow_mem_map_pow {S : Type*} [CommRing S]
    [Algebra (exampleRing k) S] (c : S) {z : exampleRing k} (hz : z ∈ adicIdeal k) {n e : ℕ}
    (hne : n ≤ e) :
    (c * algebraMap (exampleRing k) S z) ^ e ∈
      (adicIdeal k ^ n).map (algebraMap (exampleRing k) S) := by
  rw [mul_pow, ← map_pow]
  refine Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ?_)
  rw [← Nat.add_sub_of_le hne, pow_add]
  exact Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ (Ideal.pow_mem_pow hz n)

/-- **`gᵉ → 0`, on the chart `D(x)`.** The `e`-th power of `t/x` lies in `Iⁿ·A[1/x]` for every
`n ≤ e`, because `tᵉ ∈ Iⁿ`. -/
@[stacks 0EH8 "g^e dies modulo I^n for n ≤ e, on the chart D(x)"]
theorem pow_rationalFunctionAwayX_mem_map_pow (e n : ℕ) (hne : n ≤ e) :
    rationalFunctionAwayX k ^ e ∈
      (adicIdeal k ^ n).map (algebraMap (exampleRing k) (Localization.Away (coordX k))) := by
  exact mul_algebraMap_pow_mem_map_pow k _ (coordT_mem_adicIdeal k) hne

/-- **`gᵉ → 0`, on the chart `D(y)`.** The `e`-th power of `s/y` lies in `Iⁿ·A[1/y]` for every
`n ≤ e`, because `sᵉ ∈ Iⁿ`. -/
@[stacks 0EH8 "g^e dies modulo I^n for n ≤ e, on the chart D(y)"]
theorem pow_rationalFunctionAwayY_mem_map_pow (e n : ℕ) (hne : n ≤ e) :
    rationalFunctionAwayY k ^ e ∈
      (adicIdeal k ^ n).map (algebraMap (exampleRing k) (Localization.Away (coordY k))) := by
  exact mul_algebraMap_pow_mem_map_pow k _ (coordS_mem_adicIdeal k) hne

/-! ### `cd(A, I) = 2` -/

private theorem cohomologicalDimension_le_two :
    cohomologicalDimension (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k) (adicIdeal_fg k) ≤ 2 := by
  classical
  refine cohomologicalDimension_le_card_generators (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k)
    (adicIdeal_fg k) (fun i : Fin 2 => if i = 0 then coordS k else coordT k) ?_
  have hrange : (Set.range fun i : Fin 2 => if i = 0 then coordS k else coordT k) =
      {coordS k, coordT k} := by
    ext z
    simp only [Set.mem_range, Set.mem_insert_iff, Set.mem_singleton_iff]
    refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
    · rintro ⟨i, rfl⟩
      fin_cases i <;> simp
    · rintro (rfl | rfl)
      · exact ⟨0, by simp⟩
      · exact ⟨1, by simp⟩
  rw [hrange, adicIdeal]

/-- The specialization `x, y ↦ 0` of `k[x,y][[s,t]]` onto `k[[s]][[t]]`. -/
private def specializeAmbient : ambient k →+* PowerSeries (PowerSeries k) :=
  (PowerSeries.map
      ((PowerSeries.map (MvPowerSeries.isEmptyEquiv (Fin 0) k).toRingHom).comp
        (MvPowerSeries.finSuccEquiv k 0).toRingHom)).comp
    ((MvPowerSeries.finSuccEquiv k 1).toRingHom.comp
      (MvPowerSeries.map (MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom (RingHom.id k) fun _ => (0 : k))))

private theorem specializeAmbient_relation : specializeAmbient k (relation k) = 0 := by
  simp [specializeAmbient, relation, ambientX, ambientY, ambientS, ambientT]

/-- The specialization `x, y ↦ 0`, descended to `A`; it identifies `A/(x,y)` with
`k[[s]][[t]]`. -/
private def specializeCoords : exampleRing k →+* PowerSeries (PowerSeries k) :=
  Ideal.Quotient.lift _ (specializeAmbient k) (by
    intro z hz
    refine Submodule.span_induction (p := fun w _ => specializeAmbient k w = 0) ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ hz
    · intro w hw
      rw [Set.mem_singleton_iff] at hw
      rw [hw, specializeAmbient_relation]
    · simp
    · intro a b _ _ ha hb
      rw [map_add, ha, hb, add_zero]
    · intro a b _ hb
      rw [smul_eq_mul, map_mul, hb, mul_zero])

private theorem specializeCoords_coordS : specializeCoords k (coordS k) = PowerSeries.X := by
  simp [specializeCoords, coordS, specializeAmbient, ambientS,
    MvPowerSeries.finSuccEquiv_X_zero]

private theorem specializeCoords_coordT :
    specializeCoords k (coordT k) = PowerSeries.C (PowerSeries.X : PowerSeries k) := by
  have h := MvPowerSeries.finSuccEquiv_X_succ (R := k) (n := 1) (0 : Fin 1)
  simp only [Fin.succ_zero_eq_one] at h
  simp [specializeCoords, coordT, specializeAmbient, ambientT, h,
    MvPowerSeries.finSuccEquiv_X_zero]

private theorem maximalIdeal_powerSeries_powerSeries :
    IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (PowerSeries (PowerSeries k)) =
      Ideal.span {PowerSeries.X, PowerSeries.C (PowerSeries.X : PowerSeries k)} := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
  · intro f hf
    have hf0 : PowerSeries.constantCoeff (PowerSeries.constantCoeff f) = 0 := by
      simpa only [IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal, mem_nonunits_iff,
        PowerSeries.isUnit_iff_constantCoeff, isUnit_iff_ne_zero, not_not] using hf
    obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := PowerSeries.X_dvd_iff.mpr hf0
    obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ : PowerSeries.X ∣ f - PowerSeries.C (PowerSeries.constantCoeff f) :=
      PowerSeries.X_dvd_iff.mpr (by simp)
    have hf' : f = PowerSeries.X * b + PowerSeries.C PowerSeries.X * PowerSeries.C a := by
      rw [← map_mul, ← ha, ← hb]; ring
    rw [hf']
    exact Ideal.add_mem _ (Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ (Ideal.subset_span (by simp)))
      (Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ (Ideal.subset_span (by simp)))
  · rw [Ideal.span_le]
    intro f hf
    simp only [Set.mem_insert_iff, Set.mem_singleton_iff] at hf
    rcases hf with rfl | rfl <;>
      simp [IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal, PowerSeries.isUnit_iff_constantCoeff]

private theorem map_adicIdeal_eq_maximalIdeal :
    (adicIdeal k).map (specializeCoords k) =
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (PowerSeries (PowerSeries k)) := by
  rw [adicIdeal, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_insert_eq, Set.image_singleton,
    specializeCoords_coordS, specializeCoords_coordT, maximalIdeal_powerSeries_powerSeries]

private theorem exists_ringKrullDim_powerSeries_powerSeries :
    ∃ n : ℕ, ringKrullDim (PowerSeries (PowerSeries k)) = (n : WithBot ℕ∞) ∧ 2 ≤ n := by
  obtain ⟨d, hd⟩ :=
    WithBot.ne_bot_iff_exists.mp (ringKrullDim_ne_bot (R := PowerSeries (PowerSeries k)))
  have hdtop : d ≠ ⊤ := fun h =>
    ringKrullDim_ne_top (R := PowerSeries (PowerSeries k)) (hd.symm.trans (by simp [h]))
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := ENat.ne_top_iff_exists.mp hdtop
  have hdim : ringKrullDim (PowerSeries (PowerSeries k)) = (n : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
    rw [← hd, ← hn]; rfl
  refine ⟨n, hdim, ?_⟩
  have h₁ : (1 : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ ringKrullDim (PowerSeries k) := by
    have h := ringKrullDim_succ_le_ringKrullDim_powerseries (R := k)
    rwa [ringKrullDim_eq_zero_of_field k, zero_add] at h
  have h₂ := ringKrullDim_succ_le_ringKrullDim_powerseries (R := PowerSeries k)
  have h₃ : (2 : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ ringKrullDim (PowerSeries (PowerSeries k)) := by
    refine le_trans ?_ h₂
    have h4 : (2 : WithBot ℕ∞) = 1 + 1 := by norm_num
    rw [h4]
    exact add_le_add h₁ le_rfl
  rw [hdim] at h₃
  exact_mod_cast h₃

private theorem two_le_cohomologicalDimension :
    2 ≤ cohomologicalDimension (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k) (adicIdeal_fg k) := by
  obtain ⟨n, hdim, hn2⟩ := exists_ringKrullDim_powerSeries_powerSeries k
  have hmB : (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (PowerSeries (PowerSeries k))).FG :=
    Ideal.fg_of_isNoetherianRing _
  have hcdB : cohomologicalDimension (PowerSeries (PowerSeries k))
      (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (PowerSeries (PowerSeries k))) hmB = (n : ℤ) :=
    cohomologicalDimension_maximalIdeal_eq' _ hmB n hdim
  have hc := cohomologicalDimension_map_le (specializeCoords k) (adicIdeal k) (adicIdeal_fg k)
  rw [cohomologicalDimension_congr ((adicIdeal_fg k).map (specializeCoords k)) hmB
    (map_adicIdeal_eq_maximalIdeal k), hcdB] at hc
  exact (show (2 : ℤ) ≤ (n : ℤ) by exact_mod_cast hn2).trans hc

/-- **`cd(A, I) = 2`.** The ideal `I = (s,t)` of `A = k[x,y][[s,t]]/(xs - yt)` has
cohomological dimension two: at most two because `I` has two generators (Stacks 0DX9), and at
least two because specializing `x, y ↦ 0` carries `I` onto the maximal ideal of `k[[s]][[t]]`,
whose cohomological dimension is its Krull dimension (Stacks 0DXE), and that is at least two.

This is why Stacks 0EH7 — which concludes that the limit topology on `lim Hᵖ(X, ℱₙ)` is
`I`-adic — does not apply: that result needs `cd(A, I) = 1`. -/
@[stacks 0EH8 "cd(A, I) = 2, so the cd = 1 hypothesis of Stacks 0EH7 is sharp"]
theorem cohomologicalDimension_adicIdeal_eq_two :
    cohomologicalDimension (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k) (adicIdeal_fg k) = 2 :=
  le_antisymm (cohomologicalDimension_le_two k) (two_le_cohomologicalDimension k)

/-! ### The punctured spectrum `X`, and the element `g = t/x = s/y` as a genuine section -/

open Stacks.Algebraization CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

/-- The open complement `Spec(A) ∖ V(𝔞)`, as an open subscheme of `Spec A`. -/
abbrev puncturedSpectrumOpens :
    (AlgebraicGeometry.Spec (CommRingCat.of (exampleRing k))).Opens :=
  complementZeroLocus (exampleRing k) (puncturingIdeal k)

/-- The scheme `X = Spec(A) ∖ V(𝔞)` underlying the example. -/
abbrev puncturedSpectrum : AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.{u} :=
  (puncturedSpectrumOpens k : AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme)

/-- The canonical ring map `A ⟶ Γ(X, 𝒪_X)`, through which the ideals of `A` act on sections
of the structure sheaf of `X`. -/
def structureMap :
    exampleRing k →+* (puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.obj
      (Opposite.op (⊤ : (puncturedSpectrum k).Opens)) :=
  ((AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of (exampleRing k))).inv ≫
    (puncturedSpectrumOpens k).ι.appTop).hom

/-- A point of `X` lies in `D(structureMap r)` iff `r` avoids its prime ideal. -/
theorem mem_basicOpen_structureMap (x : puncturedSpectrum k) (r : exampleRing k) :
    x ∈ (puncturedSpectrum k).basicOpen (structureMap k r) ↔ r ∉ x.1.asIdeal := by
  unfold structureMap
  rw [CommRingCat.hom_comp, RingHom.comp_apply,
    ← AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.preimage_basicOpen_top (puncturedSpectrumOpens k).ι
    ((AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of (exampleRing k))).inv r),
    AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.mem_preimage]
  show (x.1 : AlgebraicGeometry.Spec (CommRingCat.of (exampleRing k))) ∈
      (AlgebraicGeometry.Spec (CommRingCat.of (exampleRing k))).basicOpen
        ((AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of (exampleRing k))).inv r) ↔
      r ∉ x.1.asIdeal
  rw [AlgebraicGeometry.basicOpen_eq_of_affine]
  exact PrimeSpectrum.mem_basicOpen r x.1

/-! ### The neighbourhood `V = D(x) ∪ D(y)`, as an `OpensNearVanishing` -/

/-- **The neighbourhood `V` of Stacks 0EH8, as an `OpensNearVanishing`.** The open
`D(x) ∪ D(y)` of `X`, shown to contain every point of `X` at which `I` vanishes by
`notMem_or_notMem_of_adicIdeal_le`. -/
def nearVanishingOpen :
    Stacks.Algebraization.OpensNearVanishing (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k)
      (puncturingIdeal k) where
  openSet := (puncturedSpectrum k).basicOpen (structureMap k (coordX k)) ⊔
    (puncturedSpectrum k).basicOpen (structureMap k (coordY k))
  contains_vanishing x hx := by
    have hp : ¬ puncturingIdeal k ≤ x.1.asIdeal := fun h =>
      x.2 ((PrimeSpectrum.mem_zeroLocus x.1 (puncturingIdeal k : Set (exampleRing k))).mpr
        (by exact_mod_cast h))
    rw [TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_sup]
    rcases notMem_or_notMem_of_adicIdeal_le k x.1 hp hx with h | h
    · exact Or.inl ((mem_basicOpen_structureMap k x (coordX k)).2 h)
    · exact Or.inr ((mem_basicOpen_structureMap k x (coordY k)).2 h)

/-! ### `D(x)` and `D(y)` are affine opens of `X` -/

/-- **`D(r)` is an affine open of `X`, for `r ∈ 𝔞`.** `X.basicOpen (structureMap k r)` is the
preimage, under the open immersion `X ⟶ Spec A`, of the affine basic open `D(r)` of `Spec A`
itself; the hypothesis `r ∈ 𝔞` makes that preimage the *whole* basic open, since a point where
`r` is a unit cannot lie in `V(𝔞) ⊇ V(r)`. -/
private theorem isAffineOpen_basicOpen_structureMap {r : exampleRing k}
    (hr : r ∈ puncturingIdeal k) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen
      ((puncturedSpectrum k).basicOpen (structureMap k r)) := by
  have heq : structureMap k r =
      (puncturedSpectrumOpens k).ι.appTop
        ((AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of (exampleRing k))).inv r) := by
    unfold structureMap
    rw [CommRingCat.hom_comp, RingHom.comp_apply]
  rw [heq, ← AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.preimage_basicOpen_top]
  refine AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen.preimage_of_isOpenImmersion
    ((AlgebraicGeometry.isAffineOpen_top _).basicOpen _) _ ?_
  rw [AlgebraicGeometry.basicOpen_eq_of_affine, AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Opens.opensRange_ι]
  intro p hp hcon
  exact (PrimeSpectrum.mem_basicOpen r p).mp hp
    ((PrimeSpectrum.mem_zeroLocus p (puncturingIdeal k : Set (exampleRing k))).mp hcon hr)

/-- **`D(x)` is an affine open of `X`.** -/
theorem isAffineOpen_basicOpen_structureMap_coordX :
    AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen
      ((puncturedSpectrum k).basicOpen (structureMap k (coordX k))) :=
  isAffineOpen_basicOpen_structureMap k (Ideal.subset_span (by simp))

/-- **`D(y)` is an affine open of `X`.** -/
theorem isAffineOpen_basicOpen_structureMap_coordY :
    AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen
      ((puncturedSpectrum k).basicOpen (structureMap k (coordY k))) :=
  isAffineOpen_basicOpen_structureMap k (Ideal.subset_span (by simp))

/-! ### The sections `g = t/x = s/y`, as genuine sections of the structure sheaf of `X` -/

/-- The ring map `A ⟶ Γ(U, 𝒪_X)` for an open `U` of `X`, through which `A` acts on sections
over `U`: `structureMap` followed by restriction to `U`. -/
def structureMapAt (U : (puncturedSpectrum k).Opens) :
    exampleRing k →+* (puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.obj (Opposite.op U) :=
  ((puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : U ≤ ⊤)).op).hom.comp (structureMap k)

/-- Restricting `structureMap k (coordX k)` to its own basic open makes it a unit: this is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace.isUnit_res_basicOpen`, since `X.basicOpen (structureMap k
(coordX k))` is literally the basic open of that global section. -/
theorem isUnit_structureMapAt_coordX :
    IsUnit (structureMapAt k ((puncturedSpectrum k).basicOpen (structureMap k (coordX k)))
      (coordX k)) :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace.isUnit_res_basicOpen
    (X := (puncturedSpectrum k).toRingedSpace) (structureMap k (coordX k))

/-- Restricting `structureMap k (coordY k)` to its own basic open makes it a unit. -/
theorem isUnit_structureMapAt_coordY :
    IsUnit (structureMapAt k ((puncturedSpectrum k).basicOpen (structureMap k (coordY k)))
      (coordY k)) :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace.isUnit_res_basicOpen
    (X := (puncturedSpectrum k).toRingedSpace) (structureMap k (coordY k))

/-- The section `g = t/x` of `𝒪_X` on `D(x)`, as the image of `rationalFunctionAwayX` under
the universal property of the localization `A[1/x]`, through the ring map `A ⟶ Γ(D(x), 𝒪_X)`
that inverts `x`. -/
noncomputable def sectionX :
    (puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.obj
      (Opposite.op ((puncturedSpectrum k).basicOpen (structureMap k (coordX k)))) :=
  IsLocalization.lift (M := Submonoid.powers (coordX k))
    (S := Localization.Away (coordX k))
    (g := structureMapAt k ((puncturedSpectrum k).basicOpen (structureMap k (coordX k))))
    (fun y => by
      obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := y.2
      rw [← hn, map_pow]
      exact (isUnit_structureMapAt_coordX k).pow n)
    (rationalFunctionAwayX k)

/-- The section `g = s/y` of `𝒪_X` on `D(y)`, as the image of `rationalFunctionAwayY` under
the universal property of the localization `A[1/y]`. -/
noncomputable def sectionY :
    (puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.obj
      (Opposite.op ((puncturedSpectrum k).basicOpen (structureMap k (coordY k)))) :=
  IsLocalization.lift (M := Submonoid.powers (coordY k))
    (S := Localization.Away (coordY k))
    (g := structureMapAt k ((puncturedSpectrum k).basicOpen (structureMap k (coordY k))))
    (fun y => by
      obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := y.2
      rw [← hn, map_pow]
      exact (isUnit_structureMapAt_coordY k).pow n)
    (rationalFunctionAwayY k)

/-- Applying the localization lift to `x · g = t` in `A[1/x]` (or any `A[1/r]`) gives the same
identity for the lifted element. -/
private theorem structureMapAt_mul_lift {r c : exampleRing k}
    {U : (puncturedSpectrum k).Opens}
    (hu : ∀ y : Submonoid.powers r, IsUnit (structureMapAt k U y))
    {g : Localization.Away r}
    (h : algebraMap (exampleRing k) (Localization.Away r) r * g =
      algebraMap (exampleRing k) (Localization.Away r) c) :
    structureMapAt k U r * IsLocalization.lift hu g = structureMapAt k U c := by
  simpa [IsLocalization.lift_eq] using congrArg (IsLocalization.lift hu) h

/-- **`g = t/x` on `D(x)`, as a genuine section.** -/
theorem structureMapAt_coordX_mul_sectionX :
    structureMapAt k _ (coordX k) * sectionX k = structureMapAt k _ (coordT k) := by
  exact structureMapAt_mul_lift k _ (coordX_mul_rationalFunctionAwayX k)

/-- **`g = s/y` on `D(y)`, as a genuine section.** -/
theorem structureMapAt_coordY_mul_sectionY :
    structureMapAt k _ (coordY k) * sectionY k = structureMapAt k _ (coordS k) := by
  exact structureMapAt_mul_lift k _ (coordY_mul_rationalFunctionAwayY k)

/-! ### Agreement of the two charts on their overlap -/

/-- The morphism `A ⟶ Γ(U, 𝒪_X)` in `CommRingCat` underlying `structureMapAt`: `structureMap`
followed by restriction to `U`. -/
def structureMapHomAt (U : (puncturedSpectrum k).Opens) :
    CommRingCat.of (exampleRing k) ⟶ (puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.obj (Opposite.op U) :=
  CommRingCat.ofHom (structureMap k) ≫
    (puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : U ≤ ⊤)).op

/-- `structureMapAt k U` is the ring hom underlying `structureMapHomAt k U`. -/
theorem structureMapAt_eq_hom (U : (puncturedSpectrum k).Opens) :
    structureMapAt k U = (structureMapHomAt k U).hom := by
  unfold structureMapAt structureMapHomAt
  rw [CommRingCat.hom_comp]
  rfl

/-- `structureMapAt` is compatible with restriction: computing it on a smaller open is the
same as computing it on a larger one and restricting. -/
theorem structureMapHomAt_res {U U' : (puncturedSpectrum k).Opens} (h : U' ≤ U) :
    structureMapHomAt k U ≫ (puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op =
      structureMapHomAt k U' := by
  unfold structureMapHomAt
  rw [Category.assoc, ← (puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.map_comp]
  congr 2

/-- Restricting `structureMapAt k U a` to a smaller open `U'` gives `structureMapAt k U' a`. -/
theorem structureMapAt_res {U U' : (puncturedSpectrum k).Opens} (h : U' ≤ U) (a : exampleRing k) :
    (puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op (structureMapAt k U a) =
      structureMapAt k U' a := by
  rw [structureMapAt_eq_hom, structureMapAt_eq_hom, ← structureMapHomAt_res k h]
  rfl

/-- The overlap `D(x) ⊓ D(y)` of the two charts on which `g` is defined. -/
abbrev overlapXY : (puncturedSpectrum k).Opens :=
  (puncturedSpectrum k).basicOpen (structureMap k (coordX k)) ⊓
    (puncturedSpectrum k).basicOpen (structureMap k (coordY k))

/-- A unit `structureMapAt k U a` stays a unit on every smaller open `U'`. -/
private theorem isUnit_structureMapAt_of_le {U U' : (puncturedSpectrum k).Opens} (h : U' ≤ U)
    {a : exampleRing k} (ha : IsUnit (structureMapAt k U a)) : IsUnit (structureMapAt k U' a) := by
  rw [← structureMapAt_res k h]
  exact ha.map ((puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op).hom

/-- Restricting `structureMapAt k U a * b = structureMapAt k U c` to a smaller open `U'`. -/
private theorem structureMapAt_mul_res {U U' : (puncturedSpectrum k).Opens} (h : U' ≤ U)
    {a c : exampleRing k} {b : (puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.obj (op U)}
    (hb : structureMapAt k U a * b = structureMapAt k U c) :
    structureMapAt k U' a * (puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op b =
      structureMapAt k U' c := by
  have := congrArg ((puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op) hb
  rwa [map_mul, structureMapAt_res, structureMapAt_res] at this

/-- `x` is a unit on the overlap `D(x) ⊓ D(y)`. -/
theorem isUnit_structureMapAt_overlap_coordX :
    IsUnit (structureMapAt k (overlapXY k) (coordX k)) := by
  exact isUnit_structureMapAt_of_le k inf_le_left (isUnit_structureMapAt_coordX k)

/-- `y` is a unit on the overlap `D(x) ⊓ D(y)`. -/
theorem isUnit_structureMapAt_overlap_coordY :
    IsUnit (structureMapAt k (overlapXY k) (coordY k)) := by
  exact isUnit_structureMapAt_of_le k inf_le_right (isUnit_structureMapAt_coordY k)

/-- Restricting the defining identity of `sectionX` to the overlap `D(x) ⊓ D(y)`. -/
theorem structureMapAt_overlap_coordX_mul_resSectionX :
    structureMapAt k (overlapXY k) (coordX k) *
        (puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.map (homOfLE (inf_le_left : overlapXY k ≤ _)).op
          (sectionX k) =
      structureMapAt k (overlapXY k) (coordT k) := by
  exact structureMapAt_mul_res k _ (structureMapAt_coordX_mul_sectionX k)

/-- Restricting the defining identity of `sectionY` to the overlap `D(x) ⊓ D(y)`. -/
theorem structureMapAt_overlap_coordY_mul_resSectionY :
    structureMapAt k (overlapXY k) (coordY k) *
        (puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.map (homOfLE (inf_le_right : overlapXY k ≤ _)).op
          (sectionY k) =
      structureMapAt k (overlapXY k) (coordS k) := by
  exact structureMapAt_mul_res k _ (structureMapAt_coordY_mul_sectionY k)

/-- **The two charts of `g` agree on their overlap `D(x) ⊓ D(y)`.** The restriction of
`sectionX` to the overlap equals the restriction of `sectionY`: both solve
`x · (-) = t` and `y · (-) = s` there (after restriction), so
`rationalFunctionAway_eq_of_isUnit` identifies them. -/
theorem res_sectionX_eq_res_sectionY :
    (puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.map (homOfLE (inf_le_left : overlapXY k ≤ _)).op
        (sectionX k) =
      (puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.map (homOfLE (inf_le_right : overlapXY k ≤ _)).op
        (sectionY k) := by
  let : Algebra (exampleRing k)
      ((puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.obj (Opposite.op (overlapXY k))) :=
    (structureMapAt k (overlapXY k)).toAlgebra
  exact rationalFunctionAway_eq_of_isUnit k
    (isUnit_structureMapAt_overlap_coordX k) (isUnit_structureMapAt_overlap_coordY k) _ _
    (structureMapAt_overlap_coordX_mul_resSectionX k)
    (structureMapAt_overlap_coordY_mul_resSectionY k)

/-! ### The glued section `g`, on `V = D(x) ∪ D(y)` -/

/-- **`g` as a genuine section of `𝒪_X` over `V = D(x) ∪ D(y)`.** The rational function
`g = t/x = s/y` of Stacks 0EH8 is regular on the neighbourhood `V` of `V(I𝒪_X)`: it is glued
from `sectionX` and `sectionY`, which agree on the overlap by `res_sectionX_eq_res_sectionY`,
via the sheaf condition for two opens. -/
@[stacks 0EH8 "the section g"]
noncomputable def sectionG :
    (puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.obj (Opposite.op (nearVanishingOpen k).openSet) :=
  ((puncturedSpectrum k).sheaf.objSupIsoProdEqLocus
      ((puncturedSpectrum k).basicOpen (structureMap k (coordX k)))
      ((puncturedSpectrum k).basicOpen (structureMap k (coordY k)))).inv
    ⟨(sectionX k, sectionY k), res_sectionX_eq_res_sectionY k⟩

/-- The restriction of `sectionG` to `D(x)` is `sectionX`. -/
theorem res_sectionG_basicOpenX :
    (puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.map (homOfLE le_sup_left).op (sectionG k) = sectionX k :=
  TopCat.Sheaf.objSupIsoProdEqLocus_inv_fst (puncturedSpectrum k).sheaf _ _ _

/-- The restriction of `sectionG` to `D(y)` is `sectionY`. -/
theorem res_sectionG_basicOpenY :
    (puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.map (homOfLE le_sup_right).op (sectionG k) = sectionY k :=
  TopCat.Sheaf.objSupIsoProdEqLocus_inv_snd (puncturedSpectrum k).sheaf _ _ _

/-! ### `M = lim H⁰(X, 𝒪_X/IⁿM)`, and `g` as a formal section -/

/-- The unit module of the structure sheaf of `X`, the module whose quotients by `Iⁿ` are
Stacks 0EH8's `ℱₙ = 𝒪_X/Iⁿ𝒪_X`. -/
noncomputable def formalModule : (puncturedSpectrum k).Modules :=
  SheafOfModules.unit (puncturedSpectrum k).ringCatSheaf

/-- **`M`, Stacks 0EH8's inverse limit of formal sections.** The limit of
`n ↦ Γ(X, 𝒪_X/Iⁿ𝒪_X)`. -/
noncomputable def formalLimitModule : Ab.{u} :=
  limit (formalSections (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k) (puncturingIdeal k) (formalModule k))

/-- The power `gᵉ`, as a section over the neighbourhood `nearVanishingOpen k`. -/
noncomputable def sectionGFormal (e : ℕ) :
    (sectionsNearVanishing (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k) (puncturingIdeal k)
        (formalModule k)).obj (nearVanishingOpen k) :=
  sectionG k ^ e

/-! ### The omitted computation: `gᵉ ∈ Iⁿ·M` near the formal locus, for `n ≤ e` -/

open Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions in
/-- **Affine-locally, the ideal sheaf `I·𝒪_X` of the formal neighbourhood is generated by
`structureMapAt`.** On an affine open `U` of `X`, the ideal of `I·𝒪_X` is the extension of `I`
along `structureMapAt k U`. -/
theorem idealSheafNearVanishing_ideal_eq_map_structureMapAt
    (U : (puncturedSpectrum k).affineOpens) :
    (idealSheafNearVanishing (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k) (puncturingIdeal k)).ideal U =
      Ideal.map (structureMapAt k U.1) (adicIdeal k) := by
  have h1 : (idealSheafNearVanishing (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k) (puncturingIdeal k)).ideal U =
      Ideal.map ((puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top (a := U.1))).op).hom
        (baseIdeal (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k) (puncturedSpectrumOpens k).ι) :=
    baseIdealSheaf_ideal (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k) (puncturedSpectrumOpens k).ι U
  have h2 : baseIdeal (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k) (puncturedSpectrumOpens k).ι =
      Ideal.map (structureMap k) (adicIdeal k) := rfl
  rw [h1, h2, Ideal.map_map]
  rfl

/-- A section over an affine open `U` lying in `Iⁿ·Γ(U, 𝒪_X)` lies in `Iⁿ·M` over `U`. -/
private theorem mem_idealPowerMultiple_of_mem_map {n : ℕ}
    (U : (puncturedSpectrum k).affineOpens) {a : (puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.obj (op U.1)}
    (ha : a ∈ Ideal.map (structureMapAt k U.1) (adicIdeal k ^ n)) :
    a ∈ (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPower.idealPowerMultiple
          (idealSheafNearVanishing (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k)
            (puncturingIdeal k)) n (formalModule k)).toSubmodule.obj (op U.1) := by
  refine Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPower.le_idealPowerMultiple_obj _ n (formalModule k) U ?_
  rw [idealSheafNearVanishing_ideal_eq_map_structureMapAt, ← Ideal.map_pow]
  have hle : Ideal.map (structureMapAt k U.1) (adicIdeal k ^ n) ≤
      Ideal.map (structureMapAt k U.1) (adicIdeal k ^ n) •
        (⊤ : Submodule ((puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.obj (op U.1))
          ((puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.obj (op U.1))) := by
    have := Submodule.map_le_smul_top (Ideal.map (structureMapAt k U.1) (adicIdeal k ^ n))
      (LinearMap.id (R := (puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.obj (op U.1)))
    rwa [Submodule.map_id] at this
  exact hle ha

/-- Every power of `x` maps to a unit of `Γ(D(x), 𝒪_X)`. -/
theorem isUnit_structureMapAt_coordX_of_mem_powers :
    ∀ y : Submonoid.powers (coordX k),
      IsUnit (structureMapAt k ((puncturedSpectrum k).basicOpen (structureMap k (coordX k))) y) :=
  fun y => by
    obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := y.2
    rw [← hm, map_pow]
    exact (isUnit_structureMapAt_coordX k).pow m

/-- The ring map `A[1/x] ⟶ Γ(D(x), 𝒪_X)` induced by `structureMapAt` on `D(x)`. -/
def sectionXLift :
    Localization.Away (coordX k) →+*
      (puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.obj
        (op ((puncturedSpectrum k).basicOpen (structureMap k (coordX k)))) :=
  IsLocalization.lift (M := Submonoid.powers (coordX k)) (S := Localization.Away (coordX k))
    (isUnit_structureMapAt_coordX_of_mem_powers k)

/-- `sectionX` is the image of `rationalFunctionAwayX` under `sectionXLift`. -/
theorem sectionX_eq_sectionXLift :
    sectionX k = sectionXLift k (rationalFunctionAwayX k) := rfl

/-- `sectionXLift` restricts along `A ⟶ A[1/x]` to `structureMapAt` on `D(x)`. -/
theorem sectionXLift_comp_algebraMap :
    (sectionXLift k).comp (algebraMap (exampleRing k) (Localization.Away (coordX k))) =
      structureMapAt k ((puncturedSpectrum k).basicOpen (structureMap k (coordX k))) :=
  IsLocalization.lift_comp (isUnit_structureMapAt_coordX_of_mem_powers k)

/-- **The omitted computation, on the chart `D(x)`: `gᵉ ∈ Iⁿ·M` for `n ≤ e`.** Pushing
`pow_rationalFunctionAwayX_mem_map_pow` forward along `sectionXLift` identifies the ideal it
lands in with `Iⁿ·Γ(D(x), 𝒪_X)` via `idealSheafNearVanishing_ideal_eq_map_structureMapAt`, and
`sectionX k ^ e` itself with the image of `rationalFunctionAwayX k ^ e`. -/
theorem sectionX_pow_mem_idealPowerMultiple (e n : ℕ) (hne : n ≤ e) :
    sectionX k ^ e ∈
      (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPower.idealPowerMultiple
          (idealSheafNearVanishing (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k)
            (puncturingIdeal k)) n (formalModule k)).toSubmodule.obj
        (op ((puncturedSpectrum k).basicOpen (structureMap k (coordX k)))) := by
  refine mem_idealPowerMultiple_of_mem_map k
    ⟨(puncturedSpectrum k).basicOpen (structureMap k (coordX k)),
      isAffineOpen_basicOpen_structureMap_coordX k⟩ ?_
  have hmem := Ideal.mem_map_of_mem (sectionXLift k)
    (pow_rationalFunctionAwayX_mem_map_pow k e n hne)
  rw [Ideal.map_map, sectionXLift_comp_algebraMap, map_pow, ← sectionX_eq_sectionXLift] at hmem
  exact hmem

/-- Every power of `y` maps to a unit of `Γ(D(y), 𝒪_X)`. -/
theorem isUnit_structureMapAt_coordY_of_mem_powers :
    ∀ y : Submonoid.powers (coordY k),
      IsUnit (structureMapAt k ((puncturedSpectrum k).basicOpen (structureMap k (coordY k))) y) :=
  fun y => by
    obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := y.2
    rw [← hm, map_pow]
    exact (isUnit_structureMapAt_coordY k).pow m

/-- The ring map `A[1/y] ⟶ Γ(D(y), 𝒪_X)` induced by `structureMapAt` on `D(y)`. -/
def sectionYLift :
    Localization.Away (coordY k) →+*
      (puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.obj
        (op ((puncturedSpectrum k).basicOpen (structureMap k (coordY k)))) :=
  IsLocalization.lift (M := Submonoid.powers (coordY k)) (S := Localization.Away (coordY k))
    (isUnit_structureMapAt_coordY_of_mem_powers k)

/-- `sectionY` is the image of `rationalFunctionAwayY` under `sectionYLift`. -/
theorem sectionY_eq_sectionYLift :
    sectionY k = sectionYLift k (rationalFunctionAwayY k) := rfl

/-- `sectionYLift` restricts along `A ⟶ A[1/y]` to `structureMapAt` on `D(y)`. -/
theorem sectionYLift_comp_algebraMap :
    (sectionYLift k).comp (algebraMap (exampleRing k) (Localization.Away (coordY k))) =
      structureMapAt k ((puncturedSpectrum k).basicOpen (structureMap k (coordY k))) :=
  IsLocalization.lift_comp (isUnit_structureMapAt_coordY_of_mem_powers k)

/-- **The omitted computation, on the chart `D(y)`: `gᵉ ∈ Iⁿ·M` for `n ≤ e`.** The mirror of
`sectionX_pow_mem_idealPowerMultiple` on the other chart. -/
theorem sectionY_pow_mem_idealPowerMultiple (e n : ℕ) (hne : n ≤ e) :
    sectionY k ^ e ∈
      (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPower.idealPowerMultiple
          (idealSheafNearVanishing (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k)
            (puncturingIdeal k)) n (formalModule k)).toSubmodule.obj
        (op ((puncturedSpectrum k).basicOpen (structureMap k (coordY k)))) := by
  refine mem_idealPowerMultiple_of_mem_map k
    ⟨(puncturedSpectrum k).basicOpen (structureMap k (coordY k)),
      isAffineOpen_basicOpen_structureMap_coordY k⟩ ?_
  have hmem := Ideal.mem_map_of_mem (sectionYLift k)
    (pow_rationalFunctionAwayY_mem_map_pow k e n hne)
  rw [Ideal.map_map, sectionYLift_comp_algebraMap, map_pow, ← sectionY_eq_sectionYLift] at hmem
  exact hmem

/-! ### Gluing the two charts: `gᵉ ∈ Iⁿ·M` on all of `V = D(x) ∪ D(y)` -/

/-- **`gᵉ ∈ Iⁿ·M` near the formal locus, on all of `V = D(x) ∪ D(y)`, for `n ≤ e`.** Glued from
the chart computations `sectionX_pow_mem_idealPowerMultiple` and
`sectionY_pow_mem_idealPowerMultiple` via `AlgebraicGeometry.mem_submodule_of_locally_mem`: every
point of `V` lies in `D(x)` or `D(y)`, where the restriction of `gᵉ = sectionG k ^ e` is
`sectionX k ^ e` resp. `sectionY k ^ e` by `res_sectionG_basicOpenX`/`res_sectionG_basicOpenY`. -/
theorem sectionG_pow_mem_idealPowerMultiple (e n : ℕ) (hne : n ≤ e) :
    sectionG k ^ e ∈
      (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPower.idealPowerMultiple
          (idealSheafNearVanishing (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k)
            (puncturingIdeal k)) n (formalModule k)).toSubmodule.obj
        (op (nearVanishingOpen k).openSet) := by
  refine AlgebraicGeometry.mem_submodule_of_locally_mem (M := formalModule k)
    (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPower.idealPowerMultiple
      (idealSheafNearVanishing (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k) (puncturingIdeal k)) n
      (formalModule k))
    (nearVanishingOpen k).openSet (sectionG k ^ e) (fun pt hpt => ?_)
  have key : ∀ (U : (puncturedSpectrum k).Opens) (hU : U ≤ (nearVanishingOpen k).openSet)
      (a : (puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.obj (op U)),
      (puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.map (homOfLE hU).op (sectionG k) = a →
      a ^ e ∈ (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPower.idealPowerMultiple
          (idealSheafNearVanishing (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k) (puncturingIdeal k)) n
          (formalModule k)).toSubmodule.obj (op U) →
      (puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.map (homOfLE hU).op (sectionG k ^ e) ∈
        (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPower.idealPowerMultiple
          (idealSheafNearVanishing (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k) (puncturingIdeal k)) n
          (formalModule k)).toSubmodule.obj (op U) := fun U hU a ha hmem => by
    rw [map_pow, ha]
    exact hmem
  have hpt' : pt ∈ (puncturedSpectrum k).basicOpen (structureMap k (coordX k)) ⊔
      (puncturedSpectrum k).basicOpen (structureMap k (coordY k)) := hpt
  rw [TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_sup] at hpt'
  rcases hpt' with hpt | hpt
  · exact ⟨_, le_sup_left, hpt, key _ le_sup_left _ (res_sectionG_basicOpenX k)
      (sectionX_pow_mem_idealPowerMultiple k e n hne)⟩
  · exact ⟨_, le_sup_right, hpt, key _ le_sup_right _ (res_sectionG_basicOpenY k)
      (sectionY_pow_mem_idealPowerMultiple k e n hne)⟩

/-! ### `gᵉ` as a formal section, and its convergence to `0` -/

/-- **`gᵉ` as a formal section, Stacks 0EH8's element of `M = lim H⁰(X, 𝒪_X/IⁿM)`.** The
image of `sectionGFormal k e` under the canonical comparison `comparisonAt` at the
neighbourhood `nearVanishingOpen k`. -/
@[stacks 0EH8 "each power g^e gives an element of M = lim H⁰(X, ℱₙ)"]
noncomputable def formalSectionG (e : ℕ) :
    ToType (limit (formalSections (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k) (puncturingIdeal k)
      (formalModule k))) :=
  ConcreteCategory.hom
    (comparisonAt (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k) (puncturingIdeal k) (formalModule k)
      (nearVanishingOpen k))
    (sectionGFormal k e)

/-- **`gᵉ` dies in the `n`-th term of the tower as soon as `e ≥ n`.** The component of
`formalSectionG k e` at `n` is the reduction of `gᵉ` modulo `Iⁿ` on the neighbourhood
`nearVanishingOpen k`, by `comparisonAt_π`, and that reduction vanishes by
`sectionG_pow_mem_idealPowerMultiple`. -/
theorem π_formalSectionG_eq_zero (e : ℕ) (n : ℕᵒᵖ) (hne : n.unop ≤ e) :
    ConcreteCategory.hom
        (limit.π (formalSections (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k) (puncturingIdeal k)
          (formalModule k)) n) (formalSectionG k e) = 0 := by
  have hz : ConcreteCategory.hom
      (projNearVanishing (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k) (puncturingIdeal k) (formalModule k)
        (nearVanishingOpen k) n) (sectionGFormal k e) = 0 :=
    (adicProj_app_apply_eq_zero_iff
        (idealSheafNearVanishing (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k) (puncturingIdeal k))
        (formalModule k) n (nearVanishingOpen k).openSet (sectionGFormal k e)).mpr
      (sectionG_pow_mem_idealPowerMultiple k e n.unop hne)
  show ConcreteCategory.hom
      (limit.π (formalSections (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k) (puncturingIdeal k)
        (formalModule k)) n) (ConcreteCategory.hom
        (comparisonAt (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k) (puncturingIdeal k) (formalModule k)
          (nearVanishingOpen k)) (sectionGFormal k e)) = 0
  rw [← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, comparisonAt_π, ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, hz, map_zero]

/-- In the discrete topology `⊥`, the neighbourhood filter of a point is `pure` of it. -/
private theorem nhds_bot_eq_pure {α : Type*} (y : α) : @nhds α ⊥ y = pure y := by
  let : TopologicalSpace α := ⊥
  have : DiscreteTopology α := ⟨rfl⟩
  exact congrFun (nhds_discrete _) y

/-- A sequence converges to `0` in an infimum of topologies induced from discrete terms as soon
as each of its components eventually vanishes. -/
private theorem tendsto_atTop_nhds_zero_of_eventually_apply_eq_zero {J : Type*} {L : Type*}
    {P : J → Type*} [Zero L] [∀ j, Zero (P j)] (p : ∀ j, L → P j) (hp : ∀ j, p j 0 = 0)
    (x : ℕ → L) (hx : ∀ j, ∀ᶠ e in Filter.atTop, p j (x e) = 0) :
    Filter.Tendsto x Filter.atTop (@nhds L (⨅ j, TopologicalSpace.induced (p j) ⊥) 0) := by
  rw [nhds_iInf, Filter.tendsto_iInf]
  intro j
  rw [nhds_induced (T := ⊥) (p j) 0, nhds_bot_eq_pure, Filter.tendsto_comap_iff,
    Filter.tendsto_pure]
  simpa [hp j] using hx j

/-- **The limit topology on `M = lim H⁰(X, 𝒪_X/IⁿM)`.** The infimum of the topologies induced
by the projections to the (discrete) terms `Γ(X, 𝒪_X/Iⁿ𝒪_X)` of the tower. -/
@[instance_reducible]
noncomputable def limitTopologyFormalLimitModule :
    TopologicalSpace (ToType (limit (formalSections (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k)
      (puncturingIdeal k) (formalModule k)))) :=
  ⨅ n : ℕᵒᵖ, TopologicalSpace.induced
    (fun x => ConcreteCategory.hom
      (limit.π (formalSections (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k) (puncturingIdeal k)
        (formalModule k)) n) x) ⊥

/-- **`gᵉ → 0` in the limit topology, Stacks 0EH8.** For each `n`, `gᵉ` already dies in the
tower's `n`-th term as soon as `e ≥ n`, by `sectionG_pow_mem_idealPowerMultiple`. -/
@[stacks 0EH8 "g^e → 0 as e → ∞ in the limit topology on M"]
theorem tendsto_formalSectionG_atTop_nhds_zero :
    Filter.Tendsto (fun e => formalSectionG k e) Filter.atTop
      (@nhds _ (limitTopologyFormalLimitModule k) 0) :=
  tendsto_atTop_nhds_zero_of_eventually_apply_eq_zero
    (fun n x => ConcreteCategory.hom
      (limit.π (formalSections (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k) (puncturingIdeal k)
        (formalModule k)) n) x)
    (fun _ => map_zero _) (fun e => formalSectionG k e)
    (fun n => Filter.eventually_atTop.2
      ⟨n.unop, fun e he => π_formalSectionG_eq_zero k e n he⟩)

/-! ### `M` as a module over `Γ(X, 𝒪_X)`, and `gᵉ ∉ I·M` as a statement

`formalSections` is `Ab`-valued, so `limit (formalSections …)` is a bare abelian group and `I·M`
— a `Submodule` — cannot be written against it at all. Evaluating the same quotient tower through
`SheafOfModules.evaluation` instead of `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.toPresheaf` gives it its
`Γ(X, 𝒪_X)`-module structure without changing the diagram, and
`Stacks.Algebraization.ofFormalSections` carries `formalSectionG` across the comparison of the two
limits (`Stacks.Algebraization.formalSectionsLimitComparison`). On the other side of that
transport `I·M` is a genuine submodule and `gᵉ ∉ I·M` is a proposition one can write down. -/

/-- **`M = lim H⁰(X, 𝒪_X/Iⁿ𝒪_X)` with its `Γ(X, 𝒪_X)`-module structure.** The same limit as
`formalLimitModule`, taken in `ModuleCat Γ(X, 𝒪_X)` rather than in `Ab`; the two have the same
underlying abelian group, by `Stacks.Algebraization.formalSectionsLimitComparison`. -/
noncomputable abbrev formalLimitModuleCat :
    ModuleCat.{u}
      ((puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.obj (op (⊤ : (puncturedSpectrum k).Opens))) :=
  formalSectionsLimitModule (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k) (puncturingIdeal k) (formalModule k)

/-- **`gᵉ` as an element of `M` carrying its module structure.** The transport of
`formalSectionG k e` across the comparison of the two limits. It has the same components as
`formalSectionG k e`, by `Stacks.Algebraization.π_ofFormalSections`. -/
noncomputable def formalSectionGModule (e : ℕ) : ToType (formalLimitModuleCat k) :=
  ofFormalSections (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k) (puncturingIdeal k) (formalModule k)
    (formalSectionG k e)

/-- **`I·M`, Stacks 0EH8's submodule, as a genuine `Submodule`.** The multiples of `M` by the
image of `I = (s,t)` in `Γ(X, 𝒪_X)`. -/
noncomputable def adicIdealSmulFormalLimit :
    Submodule ((puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.obj (op (⊤ : (puncturedSpectrum k).Opens)))
      (ToType (formalLimitModuleCat k)) :=
  idealSmulFormalSectionsLimit (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k) (puncturingIdeal k) (formalModule k)

/-- `I·M` is cut out by the image of `I = (s,t)` under `structureMap`, the ring map `A ⟶ Γ(X,
𝒪_X)` through which the ideals of `A` act on `M`. -/
theorem adicIdealSmulFormalLimit_eq :
    adicIdealSmulFormalLimit k =
      Ideal.map (structureMap k) (adicIdeal k) •
        (⊤ : Submodule ((puncturedSpectrum k).presheaf.obj (op (⊤ : (puncturedSpectrum k).Opens)))
          (ToType (formalLimitModuleCat k))) :=
  rfl

/-- `s·m` lies in `I·M` for every formal section `m`. -/
theorem smul_coordS_mem_adicIdealSmulFormalLimit (m : ToType (formalLimitModuleCat k)) :
    structureMap k (coordS k) • m ∈ adicIdealSmulFormalLimit k :=
  mem_idealSmulFormalSectionsLimit_of_mem (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k) (puncturingIdeal k)
    (formalModule k) (coordS_mem_adicIdeal k) m

/-- `t·m` lies in `I·M` for every formal section `m`. -/
theorem smul_coordT_mem_adicIdealSmulFormalLimit (m : ToType (formalLimitModuleCat k)) :
    structureMap k (coordT k) • m ∈ adicIdealSmulFormalLimit k :=
  mem_idealSmulFormalSectionsLimit_of_mem (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k) (puncturingIdeal k)
    (formalModule k) (coordT_mem_adicIdeal k) m

/-- `gᵉ` dies in the `n`-th term of the tower for `e ≥ n`, read on the module-valued limit. -/
theorem π_formalSectionGModule_eq_zero (e : ℕ) (n : ℕᵒᵖ) (hne : n.unop ≤ e) :
    ConcreteCategory.hom
        (limit.π (formalSectionsModule (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k) (puncturingIdeal k)
          (formalModule k)) n) (formalSectionGModule k e) = 0 :=
  (π_ofFormalSections (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k) (puncturingIdeal k) (formalModule k) n
    (formalSectionG k e)).trans (π_formalSectionG_eq_zero k e n hne)

/-- **The limit topology on `M`, read on the module-valued limit.** The same infimum of induced
topologies as `limitTopologyFormalLimitModule`, with the projections of
`Stacks.Algebraization.formalSectionsModule` in place of those of `formalSections`. -/
@[instance_reducible]
noncomputable def limitTopologyFormalLimitModuleCat :
    TopologicalSpace (ToType (formalLimitModuleCat k)) :=
  ⨅ n : ℕᵒᵖ, TopologicalSpace.induced
    (fun x => ConcreteCategory.hom
      (limit.π (formalSectionsModule (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k) (puncturingIdeal k)
        (formalModule k)) n) x) ⊥

/-- **`gᵉ → 0` in the limit topology on `M`, read on the module-valued limit.** The transport of
`tendsto_formalSectionG_atTop_nhds_zero`: by `π_formalSectionGModule_eq_zero` the components of
`gᵉ` are unchanged by the transport, so they still vanish for `e ≥ n`. -/
theorem tendsto_formalSectionGModule_atTop_nhds_zero :
    Filter.Tendsto (fun e => formalSectionGModule k e) Filter.atTop
      (@nhds _ (limitTopologyFormalLimitModuleCat k) 0) :=
  tendsto_atTop_nhds_zero_of_eventually_apply_eq_zero
    (fun n x => ConcreteCategory.hom
      (limit.π (formalSectionsModule (exampleRing k) (adicIdeal k) (puncturingIdeal k)
        (formalModule k)) n) x)
    (fun _ => map_zero _) (fun e => formalSectionGModule k e)
    (fun n => Filter.eventually_atTop.2
      ⟨n.unop, fun e he => π_formalSectionGModule_eq_zero k e n he⟩)

/-- **Stacks 0EH8's clause `gᵉ ∉ I·M`, as a proposition.** The element `formalSectionGModule k e`
does not lie in the submodule `adicIdealSmulFormalLimit k`. -/
def NotMemAdicIdealSmulFormalLimit (e : ℕ) : Prop :=
  formalSectionGModule k e ∉ adicIdealSmulFormalLimit k

/-! ### The commutative algebra behind `gᵉ ∉ IM` -/

/-- **The obstruction behind `gᵉ ∉ IM`, Stacks 0EH8.** There is no solution of `y·P + x·Q = 1`
in `k[x, y]`: evaluating both sides at `x = y = 0` sends the left side to `0` and the right
side to `1`, which differ because `k` is a field.

The *untruncated* chart isomorphism `A[1/x] ≅ k[x^{±1}, y][[t]]` is false. Inverting `x` in a
power-series ring is not inverting it in the coefficients: substituting `s ↦ (y/x)t` sends
`a/xᵐ` with `a = Σ aᵢⱼ sⁱ tʲ ∈ k[x,y][[s,t]]` to the series whose `t^d`-coefficient is
`x^(-m-d) · Σ_{i+j=d} aᵢⱼ yⁱ x^(d-i)`, whose pole order in `x` is therefore at most `d + m`
for one `m` serving all `d`. So `A[1/x]` is carried into the proper subring of
`k[x^{±1}, y][[t]]` cut out by that bound — `Σ_d x^(-2d) tᵈ` is in the target and not in the
image — whereas mod `Iⁿ` only the coefficients `d < n` survive, finitely many, and every pole
order is reached. The truncated form `A[1/x]/Iⁿ ≅ k[x^{±1}, y][t]/(tⁿ)` is true: `A/Iⁿ` is the
polynomial ring `k[x,y][s,t]/((xs − yt) + (s,t)ⁿ)`
(`Stacks.Examples.NonAdicLimit.truncationEquiv`), and a polynomial ring, unlike a power series
ring, commutes with localization. -/
theorem not_isUnit_mul_add_mul (P Q : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k) :
    MvPolynomial.X 1 * P + MvPolynomial.X 0 * Q ≠ (1 : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k) := by
  intro h
  have heval := congrArg (MvPolynomial.eval (fun _ : Fin 2 => (0 : k))) h
  simp at heval

end Stacks.Examples.NonAdicLimit

end
